{"id": "19801", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=19801", "title": "Lisbon (North Dakota)", "text": "Lisbon is a town in the Coteaus and Plains area of North Dakota. It has a population of about 2,292 people. Elevation: 1,091 feet.\nUnderstand.\nThe original owners of the town site came to North Dakota from Lisbon, NY and Lisbon, IL. The farming and ranching community sits on the banks of the Sheyenne River.\nGo next.\nLisbon is at the south end of the Sheyenne Valley Scenic Byway which runs north through Valley City to Cooperstown in Griggs County."}
